::id(readme)
::export(
  type: commonmark,
  path: "README.md"
)
::meta(
  lang:      "en"
  lang_name: "English"
)

$macro.generated_by(self::path)

=[ Tomet ]

// @fixme| ファイルパスでのフィルタが望ましい。
{$ vault::docs
    .filter(d => d::filename == "readme.tmt" && exists(d::meta.lang))
    .sort(d => d::meta.lang)
    .map(d => d.link(d::meta.lang_name))
    .join(" | ")
}

Tome to me.

Tomet is a human-readable, structured markup language and Rust toolchain.
It combines clear syntax for typed data and cross-document links with multi-format export.

==[ Example ]

```tmt
`` ::id(readme)
``
`` =[ heading ]
``
`` - list #(id)
``   -. orderd
``
`` @table
`` |[ col1 ][ col2 ][ col3 ]
``
`` @callout(info)
`` | content
```

==[ Try it ]

===[ 1. Install ]

Install `sisho` and `tomet` together using the @link[Quick install](tmt:tmtroot/docs/install_tools.tmt#quick-install):

```bash
`` nix profile install github:tomet-lang/sisho#toolchain
```

===[ 2. Write hello.tmt ]

Create a document `hello.tmt`:

```tmt
`` =[ Hello, Tomet ]
``
`` Tomet is a *structured* markup language.
``
`` - a list item
``   -. an ordered child
``
`` @callout(note)
`` | A callout.
``
`` @table
`` |[ name  ][ kind     ]
`` |[ tomet ][ language ]
```

===[ 3. Check it ]

Validate and format your document:

```bash
`` sisho check .
`` sisho fix .
```

Continue with the @link[Quick Start](tmt:tmtroot/docs/quick_start.tmt).

